  "id": "COMPOUND:42370 - PROTEIN:4961",
  "verbalization": "Calcium;4-Oxopentanoate;Dihydrate is implicated in the biological activity of FaDu through a series of molecular interactions involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. These kinases are targets of multiple compounds, including Javanicoside F and 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine, all of which share a common relationship with FaDu. The evidence suggests that Calcium;4-Oxopentanoate;Dihydrate may act through a shared mechanism, potentially by modulating the activity of these kinases, which in turn influence the behavior of FaDu. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Calcium;4-Oxopentanoate;Dihydrate in regulating cellular processes through a network of protein kinases, with FaDu being a downstream target of several of these compounds. The observed scores support a consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Calcium;4-Oxopentanoate;Dihydrate interacts with FaDu remains to be fully elucidated.",
